# Database

## Engine
- PostgreSQL + EF Core
- Schema changes **only** via migrations — never silent `EnsureCreated` in prod

## Core model
```
Plan 1—* Partner
Plan 1—* Installment
Installment 1—* Payment (per partner share)
Partner ← Payment.OwnerPartnerId, Payment.PaidByPartnerId
```

Suggested columns:
- Plan: Id, OwnerUserId, Title, Description, DeliveryInstallmentId, audit
- Partner: Id, PlanId, Name, Color, DefaultPct, SortOrder
- Installment: Id, PlanId, Name, DueDate, TotalAmount, ShareType, SortOrder
- InstallmentShare (optional store): PartnerId, Amount (for custom / snapshot)
- Payment: InstallmentId, PartnerId, IsPaid, PaidAt, PaidByPartnerId, Note

## Constraints
- FK cascade: deleting Plan removes children; deleting Partner blocked if payments exist (or reassign)
- Indexes: `(PlanId)`, `(InstallmentId, PartnerId)` unique on Payment
- Money: `numeric(18,2)`
- Soft delete flags where required for audit

## Seed
- Fuzul template (1,070,000 ₺ / 20 installments) as reference seed — not the only plan
